a-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(221.4,485) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> H<sub>2</sub>O\n<br><br>So, to consume 1 mole of C<sub>x</sub> H<sub>y</sub> we need \n<br><br>(x + <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.585ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -797.5 793.6 1142.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(221.4,485) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) mole of O<sub>2</sub> gas.\n<br><br>As  both C<sub>x</sub> H<sub>y</sub> and O<sub>2</sub> are gas,\n<br><br>So avogadro's law is applicable on them.\n<br><br>At constant temperature and pressure according to avogadro's law, volume <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 778 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> mole\n<br><br>So, for 5L of C<sub>x</sub> H<sub>y</sub> the \n<br><br>volume of O<sub>2</sub> = 5(x + <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.585ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -797.5 793.6 1142.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(221.4,485) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>)\n<br><br>According to the question,\n<br><br>5(x + <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.795ex\" height=\"2.585ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -797.5 793.6 1142.5\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(221.4,485) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D466\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) = 25\n<br><b